1
00:00:06,933 --> 00:00:09,393
In seeing, there is just the seen.

2
00:00:09,473 --> 00:00:14,085
No one stands behind the eyes,
doing the seeing. That is anatta.

3
00:00:14,905 --> 00:00:17,094
Now watch a candle burn for a minute.

4
00:00:17,174 --> 00:00:22,298
The flame leans, steadies, shrinks
when the door opens, and recovers.

5
00:00:22,378 --> 00:00:26,183
Ask what is happening, and the
answer comes before any thought.

6
00:00:26,263 --> 00:00:30,712
The flame is changing. Something is
there, and something is happening to it.

7
00:00:31,530 --> 00:00:35,757
Here is the question. Even after the
arguments against it have been accepted,

8
00:00:35,837 --> 00:00:39,729
why does that picture come back,
the moment attention is off duty?

9
00:00:40,545 --> 00:00:45,659
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

10
00:00:46,477 --> 00:00:51,831
What I call the logic of dependency is
the seeing of anatta turned on everything.

11
00:00:51,911 --> 00:00:57,121
On change, on identity, on
continuity, and on the path itself.

12
00:00:57,942 --> 00:01:02,523
The picture of something that changes is
not a stray belief that one argument can

13
00:01:02,603 --> 00:01:05,023
remove. It is a way of reasoning.

14
00:01:05,103 --> 00:01:07,115
Call it the logic of substance.

15
00:01:07,195 --> 00:01:10,485
It starts with things, and
then asks what happens to them.

16
00:01:10,565 --> 00:01:13,234
Do they arise, last, move, end?

17
00:01:14,037 --> 00:01:17,394
The logic of dependency
starts one step earlier.

18
00:01:17,474 --> 00:01:21,199
It asks how anything is picked
out as a thing in the first place.

19
00:01:21,279 --> 00:01:24,772
And it finds that a thing is
picked out only in dependence.

20
00:01:24,852 --> 00:01:30,030
On parts, on causes, on contrasts,
and on the name it is picked out by.

21
00:01:30,110 --> 00:01:32,698
No thing is found standing
there before that.

22
00:01:33,518 --> 00:01:36,101
The two logics use the same words.

23
00:01:36,181 --> 00:01:39,335
Change, cause, identity, the path.

24
00:01:39,415 --> 00:01:41,794
But because they begin
in different places,

25
00:01:41,874 --> 00:01:44,992
the same words lead them
into different worlds.

26
00:01:45,851 --> 00:01:47,632
First, an honest question.

27
00:01:47,712 --> 00:01:49,630
Does anyone really think this way?

28
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:53,923
Ask people whether things have fixed
essences, and most will say no.

29
00:01:54,003 --> 00:01:56,165
Everything changes, they say.

30
00:01:56,245 --> 00:01:58,869
But the test is not what
people say when asked.

31
00:01:58,949 --> 00:02:01,305
It is what they do when
they are not asked.

32
00:02:02,121 --> 00:02:05,600
In space. Few people say space is a thing.

33
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:08,005
Yet almost everyone pictures it as one.

34
00:02:08,085 --> 00:02:11,538
A vast, empty room, which
would still be there,

35
00:02:11,618 --> 00:02:15,234
dark and waiting, if every
star were taken away.

36
00:02:15,314 --> 00:02:18,304
But space is never met
apart from distance,

37
00:02:18,384 --> 00:02:20,587
reach, and room for something.

38
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:26,094
The room that would survive the removal
of everything is not found. It is assumed.

39
00:02:26,893 --> 00:02:31,174
In time. Time is pictured as
a river, flowing on its own.

40
00:02:31,254 --> 00:02:34,041
The deadline approaches. The weekend flew.

41
00:02:34,121 --> 00:02:36,093
We spend time and run out of it.

42
00:02:36,173 --> 00:02:40,087
Yet under general anaesthetic,
three hours pass on the clock,

43
00:02:40,167 --> 00:02:42,003
and none in experience.

44
00:02:42,083 --> 00:02:44,793
No river is found that flowed by itself.

45
00:02:45,630 --> 00:02:48,227
These two pictures carry all the rest.

46
00:02:48,307 --> 00:02:51,610
The something that changes
is pictured as a passenger,

47
00:02:51,690 --> 00:02:54,952
set on a stage, carried along by a stream.

48
00:02:55,032 --> 00:02:59,780
Take away the stage and the stream,
and the passenger has nowhere to be.

49
00:03:00,610 --> 00:03:05,245
The habit is in grammar too. The
flame flickers. I have changed.

50
00:03:05,325 --> 00:03:09,498
The subject is held still, so that
the predicate can happen to it.

51
00:03:09,578 --> 00:03:11,305
It is there before language.

52
00:03:11,385 --> 00:03:15,897
Infants of a few months already
expect objects to persist when hidden.

53
00:03:15,977 --> 00:03:18,021
And it is clearest in emotion.

54
00:03:18,165 --> 00:03:24,117
Falsely accused, or suddenly praised,
an "I" appears, vivid and solid.

55
00:03:24,197 --> 00:03:27,990
In grief, someone is felt to have
vanished who was fully there,

56
00:03:28,070 --> 00:03:30,331
whatever one's philosophy says.

57
00:03:31,166 --> 00:03:33,994
So yes, we think this
way. Not all the time.

58
00:03:34,074 --> 00:03:36,888
A cook judges the dough
by how it responds.

59
00:03:36,968 --> 00:03:39,483
But the habit switches on when we explain,

60
00:03:39,563 --> 00:03:43,518
when we name, when we feel
threatened, and when we lose.

61
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:46,879
That is where the logic of
dependency has to be tested.

62
00:03:47,693 --> 00:03:49,515
What does "logic" mean here?

63
00:03:49,595 --> 00:03:53,876
Not a special logic of its own,
and not a leap beyond logic.

64
00:03:53,956 --> 00:03:56,336
It means the force of a consequence.

65
00:03:56,416 --> 00:04:01,091
Whoever proposes something existing
from its own side must say what it is.

66
00:04:01,171 --> 00:04:05,561
To say what it is, they must pick
it out by contrast and by name,

67
00:04:05,641 --> 00:04:07,327
and so make it dependent.

68
00:04:07,407 --> 00:04:09,574
The proposal undoes itself.

69
00:04:10,377 --> 00:04:13,195
It relies on the ordinary
rules of reasoning.

70
00:04:13,325 --> 00:04:17,077
Fire cannot be both one with
its fuel and other than it.

71
00:04:17,157 --> 00:04:21,601
And the famous refusals, neither
existent nor non existent,

72
00:04:21,681 --> 00:04:25,718
neither arising nor ceasing,
are not contradictions.

73
00:04:25,798 --> 00:04:27,756
They refuse a presupposition.

74
00:04:27,836 --> 00:04:29,889
Is the present king of France bald?

75
00:04:29,969 --> 00:04:34,414
Neither yes nor no, because there
is no present king of France.

76
00:04:34,494 --> 00:04:36,424
Does the self exist or not?

77
00:04:36,504 --> 00:04:39,889
Each answer assumes a bearer
with a status of its own.

78
00:04:39,969 --> 00:04:44,047
When no such bearer is found,
both answers fall together.

79
00:04:44,127 --> 00:04:46,058
Logic has not been suspended.

80
00:04:46,138 --> 00:04:48,413
The question had nothing to be about.

81
00:04:49,213 --> 00:04:50,342
Now to change.

82
00:04:50,422 --> 00:04:55,546
The logic of substance pictures change
as a noun with verbs happening to it.

83
00:04:55,626 --> 00:04:58,485
There is a flame, and the flame flickers.

84
00:04:59,297 --> 00:05:00,412
Look for the noun.

85
00:05:00,492 --> 00:05:05,535
The flame at this moment is wax vapour,
oxygen and light that were not there a

86
00:05:05,615 --> 00:05:08,334
moment ago, and will be gone the next.

87
00:05:08,414 --> 00:05:12,627
Take away the burning, and no flame
is left over to have been burning.

88
00:05:12,707 --> 00:05:15,820
But the verb is not found
apart from the noun either.

89
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:20,589
A flickering with nothing flickering is
no more available than a flame that never

90
00:05:20,669 --> 00:05:26,255
flickers. Nāgārjuna showed that walker
and walking are designated together,

91
00:05:26,335 --> 00:05:28,211
and neither is found first.

92
00:05:28,291 --> 00:05:30,308
So it is with changer and change.

93
00:05:31,138 --> 00:05:35,556
The logic of dependency does not swap
the old subject for a better one,

94
00:05:35,636 --> 00:05:39,156
such as a process, a flow, or an energy.

95
00:05:39,236 --> 00:05:41,099
Nothing is lost from the burning.

96
00:05:41,179 --> 00:05:42,947
The candle still burns down.

97
00:05:43,027 --> 00:05:46,344
You can say correctly when it
was lit, and when it went out.

98
00:05:46,424 --> 00:05:48,345
Only the passenger is let go.

99
00:05:49,153 --> 00:05:50,853
You can test this at once.

100
00:05:50,933 --> 00:05:55,214
The next time the picture of something
changing arises, look for the something.

101
00:05:55,294 --> 00:05:58,312
The sound that is fading.
The thought that is passing.

102
00:05:58,392 --> 00:06:01,369
Look for what is changing,
apart from the changing.

103
00:06:01,449 --> 00:06:03,719
The picture insists it must be there.

104
00:06:03,799 --> 00:06:07,184
The looking finds more
change, vivid and exact,

105
00:06:07,264 --> 00:06:08,955
and no changer behind it.

106
00:06:09,773 --> 00:06:14,244
Nāgārjuna's homage names
eight extremes, in four pairs.

107
00:06:14,324 --> 00:06:16,106
Arising and ceasing.

108
00:06:16,186 --> 00:06:19,407
Permanence and annihilation.
Coming and going.

109
00:06:19,487 --> 00:06:21,432
Identity and difference.

110
00:06:21,512 --> 00:06:26,405
Under the logic of substance, these are
just the questions one asks of anything.

111
00:06:26,485 --> 00:06:31,310
When did it start? Does it last, or is
it destroyed? Where did it come from?

112
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:32,849
Is it the same as that?

113
00:06:33,657 --> 00:06:36,620
Every one of them assumes
a thing with whereabouts.

114
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:40,506
A place in time, in space, or in identity,

115
00:06:40,586 --> 00:06:43,020
that belongs to it from its own side.

116
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,949
They are not eight separate errors.

117
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:47,725
They are eight ways of
asking where a thing is.

118
00:06:48,541 --> 00:06:52,537
The logic of dependency does not
answer them with a subtler thing.

119
00:06:52,617 --> 00:06:56,681
It finds that what was supposed
to have whereabouts is not found,

120
00:06:56,761 --> 00:06:59,072
and so the questions lose their object.

121
00:06:59,152 --> 00:07:02,415
No thing crossing an edge
from absent to present.

122
00:07:02,494 --> 00:07:04,507
No carrier beneath the change.

123
00:07:04,587 --> 00:07:07,985
No whereabouts before it
appeared, and none after.

124
00:07:08,065 --> 00:07:09,833
The sprout is not the seed.

125
00:07:09,913 --> 00:07:13,153
Yet it is not wholly other,
for rice yields rice.

126
00:07:13,988 --> 00:07:16,462
Here is the point that is easy to miss.

127
00:07:16,542 --> 00:07:20,280
The eight negations describe
dependent arising itself.

128
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:23,473
If a sprout could be found
arising from its seed,

129
00:07:23,553 --> 00:07:27,916
it would have an arising of its
own, and would not need to depend.

130
00:07:27,996 --> 00:07:32,454
That it depends is exactly why no
arising is found when it is sought.

131
00:07:32,534 --> 00:07:36,249
Dependence and unfindability are one fact.

132
00:07:37,066 --> 00:07:42,720
Switch off a lamp. The room is dark, and
the light went nowhere. Switch it on.

133
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:46,243
The room fills, and the
light came from nowhere.

134
00:07:47,065 --> 00:07:51,482
Now identity. Under the logic
of substance, "is it the same?"

135
00:07:51,562 --> 00:07:54,186
has an answer hidden in the thing itself.

136
00:07:54,266 --> 00:07:58,914
The logic of dependency asks
instead, the same by which criteria,

137
00:07:58,994 --> 00:08:00,440
and for which purpose?

138
00:08:01,253 --> 00:08:06,037
A ship whose every plank has been
replaced is the same ship on the register,

139
00:08:06,117 --> 00:08:09,569
and perhaps not for the museum
that kept the old planks.

140
00:08:09,649 --> 00:08:13,442
The child in the old photograph
is you, for your family,

141
00:08:13,522 --> 00:08:17,531
for your birth certificate, and for the
story that runs from that afternoon to

142
00:08:17,611 --> 00:08:18,811
this one.

143
00:08:19,342 --> 00:08:21,749
This does not make identity arbitrary.

144
00:08:21,829 --> 00:08:23,705
A forged passport fails.

145
00:08:23,785 --> 00:08:27,482
A mistaken face in a crowd
is corrected when it turns.

146
00:08:27,562 --> 00:08:31,694
What goes is only the claim that beneath
the criteria there is a sameness from the

147
00:08:31,774 --> 00:08:37,120
thing's own side. Identity is the
validity of a designation that works.

148
00:08:37,946 --> 00:08:40,842
The same shift changes
the word "conventional".

149
00:08:40,922 --> 00:08:44,116
To the logic of substance,
it sounds second rate.

150
00:08:44,196 --> 00:08:46,471
Merely agreed, less than real.

151
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:52,261
For the logic of dependency, conventional
truth is the only kind of validity there

152
00:08:52,341 --> 00:08:56,119
is, and it is fully
valid. It has standards.

153
00:08:56,199 --> 00:08:58,416
Tsongkhapa gives three checks.

154
00:08:58,496 --> 00:09:00,372
Known to ordinary cognition.

155
00:09:00,452 --> 00:09:03,769
Not overturned by further
ordinary cognition.

156
00:09:03,849 --> 00:09:06,921
Not contradicted by
analysis of the ultimate.

157
00:09:07,001 --> 00:09:09,937
The snake seen in a rope fails the second.

158
00:09:10,017 --> 00:09:13,334
A rope existing from its
own side fails the third.

159
00:09:13,414 --> 00:09:16,151
The rope as designated passes all three.

160
00:09:16,965 --> 00:09:20,771
And there is no deeper world
for convention to fall short of.

161
00:09:20,851 --> 00:09:23,855
Ultimate truth is the
emptiness of this one.

162
00:09:23,935 --> 00:09:26,110
One appearance, seen two ways.

163
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:28,746
Emptiness is not a ground beneath it.

164
00:09:28,826 --> 00:09:30,870
It is only its being dependent.

165
00:09:31,694 --> 00:09:36,465
Then continuity. If nothing carries
it, what makes a life one life?

166
00:09:36,545 --> 00:09:40,405
The logic of substance has one
answer. Something persists.

167
00:09:40,485 --> 00:09:45,301
Take it away, it expects, and only
disconnected flashes are left.

168
00:09:46,109 --> 00:09:49,371
The logic of dependency
rejects both pictures.

169
00:09:49,451 --> 00:09:52,482
Nāgasena's lamp is the classic image.

170
00:09:52,562 --> 00:09:57,333
The flame of the last watch of the night
is neither the flame of the first watch,

171
00:09:57,413 --> 00:09:58,800
nor a different flame.

172
00:09:58,880 --> 00:10:03,760
Nothing passes from one to the next, and
yet the second is not unconnected with the

173
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:05,040
first.

174
00:10:05,611 --> 00:10:08,018
A melody known by heart shows how.

175
00:10:08,098 --> 00:10:12,162
Each playing is new, and no
tune is stored between playings.

176
00:10:12,242 --> 00:10:15,123
Yet the tune is recognised
across them all.

177
00:10:15,204 --> 00:10:18,357
Habit, character and karma are like this.

178
00:10:18,437 --> 00:10:23,316
The link is valid and reliable, but
it is designated across the moments,

179
00:10:23,396 --> 00:10:27,501
not carried by something that runs
through them. So nothing is lost.

180
00:10:27,581 --> 00:10:33,072
Memory and responsibility hold. And
nothing is fixed. A habit can loosen.

181
00:10:33,152 --> 00:10:34,584
A grievance can end.

182
00:10:35,402 --> 00:10:39,018
Two objections come from
modern thought. The first.

183
00:10:39,098 --> 00:10:40,825
Isn't energy the substrate?

184
00:10:40,905 --> 00:10:44,213
It changes form, while
the total stays the same.

185
00:10:45,071 --> 00:10:47,328
Physics itself does not treat it so.

186
00:10:47,408 --> 00:10:51,771
Energy is a conserved quantity,
a number that keeps balancing,

187
00:10:51,851 --> 00:10:54,950
not a stuff poured from
one container into another.

188
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:57,532
Its amount depends on
the frame of reference.

189
00:10:57,612 --> 00:11:02,029
And in an expanding universe,
no total is conserved at all.

190
00:11:02,109 --> 00:11:07,070
When a match burns, nothing is found
leaving the match head and travelling into

191
00:11:07,150 --> 00:11:12,165
the flame. Conservation is a
regularity of the highest reliability.

192
00:11:12,245 --> 00:11:13,746
It is not a passenger.

193
00:11:14,578 --> 00:11:16,115
The second is subtler.

194
00:11:16,195 --> 00:11:21,564
If nothing is fixed, perhaps there is a
store of potentials behind appearances,

195
00:11:21,644 --> 00:11:23,411
waiting to be realised.

196
00:11:23,491 --> 00:11:26,387
That would make emptiness a new substance,

197
00:11:26,467 --> 00:11:29,041
made of possibilities instead of stuff.

198
00:11:29,870 --> 00:11:34,750
But a potential is known only through
what it becomes, and through its partner.

199
00:11:34,830 --> 00:11:38,015
Salt is soluble only in relation to water.

200
00:11:38,145 --> 00:11:41,230
"Could" is a designation
made within conditions,

201
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:43,554
not a thing waiting backstage.

202
00:11:43,634 --> 00:11:47,834
The Dzogchen word "unobstructed"
fits better than "potential".

203
00:11:47,914 --> 00:11:51,710
Nothing blocks the display, and
there is no store behind it.

204
00:11:52,530 --> 00:11:55,426
The two logics also lay
out different paths.

205
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:59,746
Under the logic of substance,
a traveller removes bad states,

206
00:11:59,826 --> 00:12:03,918
like lifting out a stone, and
holds good ones, like a coin.

207
00:12:03,998 --> 00:12:06,422
And the effort hardens into grasping.

208
00:12:07,233 --> 00:12:12,411
Under the logic of dependency, three
things are seen. Conditions are what work.

209
00:12:12,491 --> 00:12:14,979
Anger is not a thing with its own nature.

210
00:12:15,059 --> 00:12:19,680
Change the attention, the reading,
the posture, and it changes.

211
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:22,778
Openness is what being
dependent already means.

212
00:12:22,858 --> 00:12:27,003
If states had their own nature,
nothing could become other than it is,

213
00:12:27,083 --> 00:12:29,082
and practice would be pointless.

214
00:12:29,162 --> 00:12:33,135
And there is nothing to hold,
and no goer apart from the going.

215
00:12:33,962 --> 00:12:39,793
One trap remains. Openness and emptiness
can quietly become the new things held.

216
00:12:39,873 --> 00:12:44,222
Nāgārjuna warns against those
who make emptiness into a view.

217
00:12:44,302 --> 00:12:46,668
Openness, too, is empty.

218
00:12:46,748 --> 00:12:49,281
It is the absence of what one was holding.

219
00:12:50,081 --> 00:12:54,416
Side by side, then. The logic
of substance starts with things.

220
00:12:54,496 --> 00:12:58,438
A carrier through change,
an essence behind identity,

221
00:12:58,518 --> 00:13:01,849
a substrate of energy,
a traveller on the path.

222
00:13:01,929 --> 00:13:06,264
The logic of dependency starts with
how anything is picked out at all.

223
00:13:06,344 --> 00:13:08,465
Change and changer named together.

224
00:13:08,545 --> 00:13:10,368
Identity by criteria.

225
00:13:10,448 --> 00:13:13,411
Convention as the only validity there is.

226
00:13:13,491 --> 00:13:17,152
And a path of arranging
conditions, with nothing to hold.

227
00:13:17,973 --> 00:13:23,178
Return to the candle. The logic of
substance asks what the flame really is,

228
00:13:23,258 --> 00:13:25,379
and where it goes when it goes out.

229
00:13:25,459 --> 00:13:30,216
The logic of dependency notices that the
flame was never anything apart from the

230
00:13:30,296 --> 00:13:34,292
burning. And the burning never
anything apart from the wax,

231
00:13:34,372 --> 00:13:37,010
the air, and the one who watches.

232
00:13:37,090 --> 00:13:38,939
Nothing is taken from the candle.

233
00:13:39,019 --> 00:13:41,892
It gives exactly as much light as before.

234
00:13:42,697 --> 00:13:46,244
And this logic is not meant
to stay a set of arguments.

235
00:13:46,324 --> 00:13:50,538
When it is seen, not only
followed, something simple happens.

236
00:13:50,618 --> 00:13:54,573
With no doer anywhere, and
nothing put in its place,

237
00:13:54,653 --> 00:13:57,100
nothing is left producing the appearing.

238
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:59,818
The candle's light, a sound, a thought.

239
00:13:59,898 --> 00:14:03,840
Each appears whole, exactly
as its conditions meet,

240
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:06,616
and owes its completeness
to nothing hidden.

241
00:14:07,421 --> 00:14:11,091
The Dzogchen tradition calls
this spontaneous presence.

242
00:14:11,171 --> 00:14:15,058
It is not uncaused, and it is
not a source behind things.

243
00:14:15,138 --> 00:14:19,093
It is dependent arising
itself, met without the fixing.

244
00:14:19,173 --> 00:14:23,554
That is why I say that dependent
arising is spontaneous presence.

245
00:14:24,369 --> 00:14:26,829
In seeing, there is just the seen.

246
00:14:26,909 --> 00:14:29,239
And in the flame, just the burning.

